    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Cyprian's mean score equals to the sum of his three test scores divided by three, which implies his test scores will be 85, 87, and 98, each time multiplied by 3 since it is 3 times the mean divided by 3. Therefore, Cyprian's mean score can be computed as the sum of these three test scores divided by three:\n\n\\[\\frac{85 + 87 + 98}{3} = 90\\]\n\nGiven that 3 their three test scores equal to 276, each test score can therefore be computed as the above mean score multiplying 3, and then finally divided through three: \n\n\\[(85, 87~and~98) = \\frac{{90\\text{ x 3}}} {3} = 90\\]\n\nGiven Cyprian's total three test scores and sum equals to 276 (i.e., 276 = 85 + 87 + 98). Using the same approach, Margaret's total three test scores and sum is 267 (i.e., 267 = 85 + 87 + 92), because 92 is a smaller number than what Cyprian included. Margaret's total score and mean score can be computed similarly as follows:\n\n\\[\\frac{{267}}{{3}} = 89\\]\n\nSince establishing formal equation for Margaret's score can be derived from the previous steps outlined, we can write the following one line solution: \\[89 = \\frac{{85 + 87 + 92 \\times 3}}{{3}}\\]\n\nSo the final answer is 89.",
